            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I don't find it weird at all. I needed to edit a lot of tabularized data today; so having one cursor per row and using `gn`-motions to edit identical values within these rows (that are in different columns) with multicursors (`vgn` and `dgn` work fine btw) came in really handy. Essentially just like what I would normally do within a single row of a table. That's exactly the kind of stuff where multiple cursors shine in my opinion.",
